{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793254699873892092,"compiled_state":{"alias":"reportable-noetic-swan","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":3},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second instance in the same close: after the [non-codebase] tag, the close was refused again because a tagged item also needs an indented 'provenance: environment=...; principal=...; privilege_posture=...; instrument=... — ...' continuation line. The verifier's remediation text never mentions this requirement, and adding the line is a further plan-text edit that stales the plan-review attestation again. So one external criterion cost three refused closes and two fresh plan reviews. AC addition: the verifier's remediation names the provenance line, and the provenance line is normalized out of plan material like the tag.","timestamp":1793244231880694001}],"created_at":1793243702455059001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"21fe4e4e-daa3-40c4-b4b4-67d979d7b8b0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2d87-7428-abcf-4bd9"}],"description":"## Observation\n\nClosing abstracted-busy-copperhead (2d87-7428-abcf-4bd9) on 2026-10-28:\n\n1. The completion verifier refused the close with one unmet criterion (a Gerrit/CI fact), and its remediation text says: for evidence outside the repository, \"mark the criterion with the exact `[non-codebase]` tag and add a comment\".\n2. I added `[non-codebase] ` to that one criterion line and recorded the evidence comment.\n3. The retried close was refused by the plan-review close gate: \"stale-material: the plan was materially edited since review — changed: description (2045 -> 2060 chars); its TEXT changed ... ticking an AC checkbox is attestation-SAFE\".\n\nSo following the verifier's own remediation invalidates the plan-review attestation, and the close then needs a fresh `review-plan` (15–20 minutes plus a billable LLM pass) for a tag that changes no plan content.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe `[non-codebase]` tag the verifier asks for is normalized out of plan-material the same way checkbox state already is, so adding it does not make the plan-review attestation stale. Or the verifier's remediation names a route that does not edit the reviewed text.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Adding or removing `[non-codebase]` on an acceptance-criterion line leaves the plan-review attestation current.\n- [ ] Any other text change on that line still makes the attestation stale.\n- [ ] A test covers both cases.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"81f2-68a2-5710-4f9a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Following the completion verifier's [non-codebase] remediation makes the plan-review attestation stale","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["bd1eecf0-a73e-460f-8f35-9df8421ee767","21fe4e4e-daa3-40c4-b4b4-67d979d7b8b0","683bea6e-338d-49cf-bc02-d0e49e96f69d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793254699873892092,"uuid":"3651616f-5ca6-4355-a906-d21923226a80"}